id: pm-w7clh6
title: update-many silently drops a null update field in both the flat and nested runAction transports instead of clearing it or refusing
description: "Found by Codex review of the GH-1655 change (pm-gh1655) and corrected by CodeRabbit on PR 1658. In runAction('update-many', ...) both spellings normalize a null update field to undefined before resolveUpdateTransportOptions sees it: { ids: [id], assignee: null, description: 'changed' } and { ids: [id], update: { assignee: null, description: 'changed' } } both change the description and silently keep the assignee (reproduced on the PR 1658 build in a sandbox). Only a direct runUpdateMany call whose update record still carries the null reaches the pm-gh1655 fold. pm-gh1655 therefore kept update-many out of the null-clear contract (PmUpdateManyActionOptions stays non-nullable)."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 3
tags[4]: bulk,pm-gh1655,sdk,update-many
created_at: "2026-11-03T23:06:21.402Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-04T07:57:55.196Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: "A null on a clearable update field (one the update unset table covers) clears it in every update-many spelling (runAction flat, runAction nested and direct runUpdateMany) exactly like a single update; it is never silently dropped; A null on a non-clearable update field (for example title) refuses naming the field in every update-many spelling, exactly as a single update refuses it; Flat and nested update-many spellings of the same request produce the same rows, clears and refusals alike, with a spec for each spelling; A flat null on a key that is a selection filter rather than an update field is refused naming the key, never applied as a clear"
parent: pm-9rgaal
risk: low
confidence: high
severity: low
expected_result: "A null on a clearable update field in a flat update-many payload clears it exactly like the nested form, and a null on a non-clearable field refuses like the nested form"
actual_result: Both runAction spellings (flat and nested) drop the null field silently while the rest of the update applies
